---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
error[uninit_read]: `total` is read here before anything is written to it
  --> tests/lint/uninit_read/bad.jai:9:12
   |
 9 |     for xs total += it;
   |            ^^^^^
   |
help: `= ---` leaves `total` holding whatever was in memory: give it a value first, or drop the `= ---`
   |
 7   sum :: (xs: [] int) -> int {
 8 ~     total: int;
 9       for xs total += it;
   |
   = note: `uninit_read` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/uninit_read

error[uninit_read]: `buffer` is read here before anything is written to it
  --> tests/lint/uninit_read/bad.jai:15:12
   |
15 |     return buffer[0];
   |            ^^^^^^
   |
help: `= ---` leaves `buffer` holding whatever was in memory: give it a value first, or drop the `= ---`
   |
13   first :: () -> u8 {
14 ~     buffer: [64] u8;
15       return buffer[0];
   |
   = note: `uninit_read` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/uninit_read

error[uninit_read]: `p` is read here before anything is written to it
  --> tests/lint/uninit_read/bad.jai:20:18
   |
20 |     print("%\n", p.x);
   |                  ^
   |
help: `= ---` leaves `p` holding whatever was in memory: give it a value first, or drop the `= ---`
   |
18   corner :: () -> int {
19 ~     p: Point;
20       print("%\n", p.x);
   |
   = note: `uninit_read` is `deny` by default
